  "interpretation": [
    "Primary drift is operator activity; ordinary within-operator partition probabilities are constrained near uniform, not fixed iid globally.",
    "Two persistent hot exceptions: train01 and holdout12. One persistent cold exception: dev07. These are not sudden partition hotspot appearance/disappearance tests.",
    "Operator probabilities use global operation clock; partition drift uses local operator access clock, so speed parameters cannot be directly compared.",
    "Different profiles/periods/pressures co-vary; per-profile summaries cannot isolate drift-speed effects.",
    "Shared threshold is not a barrier; staggered phase cases exercise BUILD/PROBE overlap.",
    "This descriptive frozen comparison is separate from main final2.1 dev108/eval72. No metadata is exposed to schedulers.",
    "All12 share write bandwidth100, read bandwidth80 bytes/us and actual Miss penalty100us. This panel does not by itself validate transfer across bandwidth ratios or hidden penalties; main-train validation is separate."
